Web search results for query: "better-auth emailVerification plugin import 2025"

Search results for query: better-auth email verification plugin 2025 email verification plugin for better-auth 2025 better-auth email verification integration 2025

Links: [{"title":"BetterAuth with Encore.ts - Complete Backend Guide","url":"https://encore.dev/blog/betterauth-tutorial"},{"title":"Email & Password","url":"https://www.better-auth.com/docs/authentication/email-password"},{"title":"Email - Better Auth","url":"https://www.better-auth.com/docs/concepts/email"},{"title":"Email OTP - Better Auth plugin","url":"https://www.better-auth.com/docs/plugins/email-otp"},{"title":"The sendVerificationOTP in the Email OTP plugin dosen't provide the user object as the og link based method","url":"https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/issues/3761"},{"title":"Options - Better Auth configuration options reference","url":"https://www.better-auth.com/docs/reference/options"},{"title":"Better Auth Email Guide: Verification & Invites with Nodemailer","url":"https://rogasper.REDACTED"}]

Based on the search results from the official Better Auth documentation and recent 2025 guides, here's what you need to know about **email verification in Better Auth**:

## Important Clarification

**Email verification is NOT a separate plugin** — it's built into the core `better-auth` package. You configure it directly in your `betterAuth()` configuration.

### Import Pattern (Core Configuration)

```typescript
import { betterAuth } from "better-auth";
// No separate plugin import needed for email verification

export const auth = betterAuth({
  emailVerification: {
    sendVerificationEmail: async ({ user, url, token }, request) => {
      void sendEmail({
        to: user.email,
        subject: "Verify your email address",
        text: `Click the link to verify your email: ${url}`,
      });
    },
    sendOnSignUp: true,              // Auto-send on signup
    autoSignInAfterVerification: true, // Auto-login after verification
    expiresIn: 3600,                 // Token expiry (1 hour)
  },
  emailAndPassword: {
    enabled: true,
    requireEmailVerification: true,  // Require verification to login
  },
});
```

## Alternative: Email OTP Plugin

If you want **OTP-based** email verification (instead of link-based), there IS a separate plugin for that:

```typescript
import { betterAuth } from "better-auth";
import { emailOTP } from "better-auth/plugins"; // Plugin import

export const auth = betterAuth({
  plugins: [
    emailOTP({
      overrideDefaultEmailVerification: true, // Use OTP instead of links
      async sendVerificationOTP({ email, otp, type }) {
        // Send OTP via email
      },
    }),
  ],
});
```

### Client-side (if using Email OTP)

```typescript
import { createAuthClient } from "better-auth/client";
import { emailOTPClient } from "better-auth/client/plugins";

export const authClient = createAuthClient({
  plugins: [emailOTPClient()],
});
```

## Key Configuration Options (2025)

| Option | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `sendVerificationEmail` | Function | Required. Sends the verification email with `user`, `url`, and `token` |
| `sendOnSignUp` | boolean | Auto-send verification email on signup |
| `sendOnSignIn` | boolean | Send verification when unverified user tries to login |
| `autoSignInAfterVerification` | boolean | Automatically sign in user after successful verification |
| `expiresIn` | number | Token validity in seconds (default: 3600) |
| `afterEmailVerification` | Function | Callback after successful verification |

**Security Note:** Avoid `await` when sending emails to prevent timing attacks. Use `void sendEmail()` or `waitUntil()` on serverless platforms.


REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.

